(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase472RuntimeBoundaryAndMemorySafety"
  :createdAt 1789340000000
  :status "done"
  :priorityOrder 1
  :summary "Runtime Boundary and Memory Safety: no shell string built from request input, every path-taking operation behind one resolved boundary check, memory that cannot be written past, and error paths that cannot report success."
  :phase "Phase472RuntimeBoundaryAndMemorySafety"
  :baseline "Verified 2026-09-12 by reading the source, after an independent scout reported them. asl.c:1481 builds a shell command by interpolating a commit message taken verbatim from the request into a double quoted string and passes it to system, with the message copied by strncpy at 1473 and never escaped; asl.c:1427 does the same shape through popen with a caller supplied file path. is_safe_path is defined once at asl.c:128 and called from exactly six sites, at 853, 901, 937, 975, 1041 and 1116; the find and grep handler beginning at 1235 is not among them and accepts an absolute directory, and the JavaScript filesystem bridge at 1829 and 1868 does not call it either. is_safe_path itself is textual only: it rejects any path containing two dots and checks that an absolute path lies under the root with a correct boundary character, but never resolves the path, so a symlink inside the workspace escapes it for read and for write, and a relative path is never prefix checked at all. asl.c:3791 clamps its copy loop to fifteen entries and then writes the null terminator at an unclamped index into a sixteen element array. sb_grow at asl.c:49 ignores realloc failure and the caller memcpys regardless. A separate whole repository audit recorded as D83WholeRepositoryAudit20260912 reported additional findings, of which two were verified as already repaired and two carried inaccurate evidence lines while their conclusions stood."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task47201" :parentId "" :phase "phase-472"
      :title "No shell command is ever built from request input"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "boundary" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789340000000 :updatedAt 1789340100000
      :motivation "A commit message arriving in an rpc step is copied into a fixed buffer and interpolated into a double quoted shell string that is handed to system. Anything that closes the quote runs as the invoking user, and system uses a shell, so the usual metacharacters all apply. The same shape appears through popen with a caller supplied path, which is additionally the only file taking operation that never reaches the boundary check. This is the most serious defect found in this programme and it sits in the operation an agent is most likely to call unattended."
      :purpose "No external command is constructed by string interpolation. Arguments are passed as an argument vector rather than through a shell, so no quoting is required and none can be escaped. Where a shell is genuinely needed, the argument is escaped by the canonical escaper that already exists in asl-text and the escaping is verified by a case containing a quote, a semicolon and a substitution."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Argument vectors in place of interpolated shell strings" "No system or popen call carrying request text" "Escaping verified by adversarial cases where a shell is unavoidable"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["rpc"] :relatedSymbols ["tools" "foreign" "edge"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81" :decision "d81" :dependsOn []
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47201"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47201.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A message containing a double quote is committed literally and nothing else runs." "A message containing a semicolon followed by a command leaves no trace of that command having executed." "A source scan finds no system or popen call whose argument was assembled from request text."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47201" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47201" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47201" :assertCount 6 :at 1789340100000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Replace interpolation with argument vectors." "Add the adversarial cases." "Scan the source for the remaining shape." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47202" :parentId "" :phase "phase-472"
      :title "One boundary check, on every path, including the JavaScript bridge"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "boundary" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789340000000 :updatedAt 1789340150000
      :motivation "The boundary check is called from six places and the operations that take a path number more than six. find and grep accept an absolute directory and walk it, so a request naming any readable directory on the host enumerates it. The JavaScript filesystem bridge reads and writes without consulting the check at all, so any evaluated module reaches past every guard the request layer applies. A check applied at six of nine doors is not a boundary."
      :purpose "Every operation that accepts a path passes it through one check before use, in the request layer and in the host bridge alike, and the set of such operations is enumerated by a source scan rather than by memory so a new operation cannot be added without one."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Every path taking operation behind the check" "The host bridge included" "The set enumerated by scan, not by memory" "A new unguarded operation fails the scan"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["is_safe_path" "js_fs_readFileSync" "js_fs_writeFileSync"] :relatedSymbols ["tools" "capabilities" "edge"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47201"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47202"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47202.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A search rooted at an absolute directory outside the workspace is refused." "A module calling the host bridge with a path outside the workspace is refused." "Adding a path taking operation without the check fails the scan."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47202" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47202" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47202" :assertCount 7 :at 1789340150000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Enumerate path taking operations." "Route every one through the check." "Scan to keep it true." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47203" :parentId "" :phase "phase-472"
      :title "The boundary check resolves the path it is checking"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "boundary" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789340000000 :updatedAt 1789340250000
      :motivation "The check is textual. It rejects two dots and verifies that an absolute path lies under the root with the correct boundary character, which is correct as far as it goes, and it never resolves the path. A symlink committed into the workspace therefore passes for reading and for writing, which turns a repository that anyone can contribute a file to into arbitrary file access. A relative path is not prefix checked at all. Directory recursion uses stat rather than lstat and keeps no visited set, so a symlink to a parent makes the walk unbounded."
      :purpose "The check resolves the path and compares the resolved result against the resolved root, so a symlink is judged by where it leads rather than by how it is spelled. Relative paths are resolved first and checked identically. Recursion does not follow directory symlinks and does not revisit."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Resolution before comparison" "Relative paths checked identically" "Symlinked directories not followed" "Recursion bounded"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["is_safe_path" "resolve_path" "walk_dir_recursive"] :relatedSymbols ["tools" "bounded" "edge"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47202"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47203"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47203.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A symlink inside the workspace pointing outside it is refused for read and for write." "A relative path that resolves outside the workspace is refused." "A directory symlink pointing at an ancestor terminates the walk rather than recurring." "A legitimate file under the root still passes, so the check is not merely stricter."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47203" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47203" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47203" :assertCount 6 :at 1789340250000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Resolve before comparing." "Use lstat and a visited set." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47204" :parentId "" :phase "phase-472"
      :title "Memory that cannot be written past, and allocations that can fail"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "memory" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789340000000 :updatedAt 1789340200000
      :motivation "The growable buffer ignores a failed reallocation and the caller copies into it regardless, so an allocation failure becomes a write past the end with request controlled bytes. The evaluator argument array clamps its copy loop to fifteen entries and then writes a terminator at an index derived from the argument count, which for a longer command line lands outside the array. A path buffer for a concatenation is half the size of the buffer holding one of its inputs, so deep paths truncate silently and a later check tests a different path than the one that will be opened."
      :purpose "Allocation failure is a signal rather than a silent state, and no copy proceeds past a failed growth. Every index written is bounded by the array rather than by an input. Buffers that hold a concatenation are at least as large as the sum of their inputs, and a truncation is an error rather than a shorter string."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Allocation failure propagated" "Every write bounded by its array" "Truncation an error, not a value" "The 31 fixed buffers reviewed against their inputs"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["sb_grow" "sb_init" "sb_append_len" "walk_dir_recursive"] :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "gates"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47201"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47204"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47204.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["An evaluator invocation with more arguments than the array holds is refused rather than writing past it." "A path longer than the concatenation buffer produces an error rather than a truncated path." "A simulated allocation failure produces an error rather than a copy."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47204" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47204" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47204" :assertCount 9 :at 1789340200000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Give growth a failure signal." "Bound every index." "Size concatenation buffers." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47205" :parentId "" :phase "phase-472"
      :title "An error path may not look like a success path"
      :kind :engine :state :done :lane "honesty" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789340000000 :updatedAt 1789340300000
      :motivation "A host write whose file could not be opened returns exactly what a successful write returns, so data loss is silent to the caller. A type check whose checker failed to load falls through to a heuristic that returns nothing and then exits zero, so an unchecked file reports as checked. A read that swallows its own failure leaves the filename in place of the file content and the parser then reports a confusing error about the path. Each of these is the same defect as the gate failures this programme has been correcting, in the runtime rather than in the gates."
      :purpose "Every operation distinguishes failure from success at its own boundary. A write that did not write raises. A check that did not run says so rather than exiting zero. A read that failed does not leave its argument in place of its result. No catch discards without either handling or re-raising."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Failure distinguishable from success at every boundary" "A check that did not run cannot report clean" "No silent discard in any catch"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/tools/engine_js.h"]
      :targetSymbols ["js_fs_writeFileSync" "runStaticTypeCheck" "getCheckerClosure"] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "semantics" "output"]
      :invariants ["D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task47204"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47205"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47205.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A write to an unwritable path raises rather than returning the success value." "With the checker module removed, a check exits non zero rather than zero and silent." "An unreadable file produces a read error rather than a parse error naming the path."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47205" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task47205" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47205" :assertCount 3 :at 1789340300000)] :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Separate the failure returns." "Fail a check that did not run." "Close the silent catches." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts [(:receipt :step 4 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task47206" :parentId "" :phase "phase-472"
      :title "The verified residue of the whole repository audit"
      :kind :remediation :state :done :lane "residue" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789340000000 :updatedAt 1789340350000
      :motivation "An independent whole repository audit recorded eight findings. Two were verified as already repaired: the tool layer that was reported returning fake success now returns an explicit unsupported error, and so does the process layer. Two carried inaccurate evidence while their conclusions held. The rest were confirmed by reading, including two commands that the configuration and a shipped script both invoke and the binary rejects."
      :purpose "Each finding of that audit is verified before it is acted on, repaired where it is real, and recorded as already repaired or as inaccurately evidenced where it is not, so the audit becomes a reconciled record rather than a standing list. The confirmed governance drift is closed by Task46401, which already requires that a surface name only commands that exist, and the confirmed contract and correctness defects are repaired against their own tests."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Each finding verified before action" "Repaired findings recorded as repaired" "Inaccurate evidence corrected rather than inherited" "The audit reconciled rather than appended to"]
      :owns [".asl/mem/reviews/D83WholeRepositoryAudit20260912.asn" "harness/src" "asl/packages/asl-text/src" "web-api-search/src" "crawler/src" "asl-contracts/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["compact-history" "validate-markup-tags"] :relatedSymbols ["gates" "concepts" "grading"]
